        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 24,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ovary</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:31:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61633,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 24,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients may present with symptoms related to a pelvic mass, or the tumour may be an incidental finding.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:31:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61634,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 24,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are uncommon tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:31:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61635,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 24,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:31:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61636,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 24,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Some endometrioid cystadenomas may represent endometriotic cysts in which the endometrial stroma is inapparent. Endometrioid adenofibromas are sometimes associated with endometriosis or an endometriotic cyst.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:31:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61637,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 24,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Endometrioid cystadenomas are usually unilocular cysts. Endometrioid adenofibromas are typically solid with a firm, white cut surface, sometimes with small cysts. They may form a nodule in the wall of an endometriotic cyst.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:31:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61638,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 24,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Endometrioid cystadenomas are cysts lined by endometrioid epithelium without underlying endometrial-type stroma. Endometrioid cystadenomas and adenofibromas are both often associated with endometriosis. Endometrioid adenofibromas are characterized by fibromatous stroma containing widely spaced, cytologically bland, endometrioid glands {8463037}. Squamous (morular or non-morular) or mucinous differentiation can occur. Dystrophic stromal calcifications may be present.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:31:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61639,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 24,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:31:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61640,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 24,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:31:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61641,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 24,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> cystadenoma: cyst lined by benign endometrioid epithelium without endometrial stroma; adenofibroma: widely spaced benign endometrioid glands associated with fibromatous stroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> endometriosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:31:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61642,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 24,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:31:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61643,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 24,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are benign.</p>",
